   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "On Sat, 24 Nov 2018 at 11:26, Cwei &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">slende...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Hello,\r<br>&gt; In the example below, patient requires three resources  before timeout. If  &#39;bed&#39; becomes unavailable, and therefore timeout cannot occur, can patientB seize &#39;nurse&#39; which is currently seized by patient?\r<br>\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "In this case, the correct order would be bed &gt; nurse &gt; doctor, which\r<br>solves your problem. And in any case, you can always use auxiliary\r<br>resources with no queue and play with the &quot;reject&quot; subtrajectories.\r<br>\r<br>Iñaki\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>&gt; a_traj&lt;- trajectory() %&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   seize(&quot;bed&quot;, 1)%&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   timeout(30) %&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   release(&quot;bed&quot;, 1)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; b_traj&lt;- trajectory() %&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   seize(&quot;nurse&quot;, 1) %&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   timeout(10) %&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   release(&quot;nurse&quot;, 1)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; new_traj&lt;-trajectory(&quot;traj&quot;) %&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   seize(&quot;doctor&quot;, 1) %&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   seize(&quot;nurse&quot;, 1) %&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   seize(&quot;bed&quot;, 1) %&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   timeout(10) %&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   release(&quot;doctor&quot;, 1) %&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   release(&quot;nurse&quot;, 1) %&gt;%\r<br>&gt;   release(&quot;bed&quot;, 1)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; env&lt;-lapply(1:1, function(i) {\r<br>&gt;   simmer() %&gt;%\r<br>&gt;     add_resource(&quot;doctor&quot;, 1) %&gt;%\r<br>&gt;     add_resource(&quot;nurse&quot;, 1) %&gt;%\r<br>&gt;     add_resource(&quot;bed&quot;, 1) %&gt;%\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;     add_generator(&quot;patientA&quot;, a_traj, at(0) ) %&gt;%\r<br>&gt;     add_generator(&quot;patient&quot;, new_traj, at(5) ) %&gt;%\r<br>&gt;     add_generator(&quot;patientB&quot;, b_traj, at(10) ) %&gt;%\r<br>&gt;     run(30)\r<br>&gt; })\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; resources&lt;- get_mon_resources(env)\r<br>&gt; arrivals&lt;- get_mon_arrivals(env, per_resource =TRUE)\r<br>&gt; plot(resources, metric =&quot;usage&quot;, c( &quot;doctor&quot;, &quot;nurse&quot;, &quot;bed&quot;),items=c(&quot;queue&quot;, &quot;server&quot;), steps = TRUE)\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>"
    ],
